  <page_number>302</page_number>
  <running_head>P. VOET</running_head>
  <bottom_margin>
    <catchword>ejus</catchword>
  </bottom_margin>
  <main_text>
    <l n="1">riculo, dum ad ejus nutum,</l>
    <l n="2">cui infensus est, gladium strin-</l>
    <l n="3">git. Si enim superior evadat,</l>
    <l n="4">vitam quidem servat, verum</l>
    <l n="5">tamen bonam famam apud</l>
    <l n="6">bonos; conscientiam bonam</l>
    <l n="7">apud Deum perdit, &amp; nihil</l>
    <l n="8">supereft, nisi ut metuat igno-</l>
    <l n="9">miniosam carnificis manum.</l>
    <l n="10">Sin pereat, unà cum existima-</l>
    <l n="11">tione vitam amittit, forte eti-</l>
    <l n="12">am æternam. Et ita posteritati</l>
    <l n="13">exemplo est, ne adeo temerariè</l>
    <l n="14">periculo sese exponat, quod</l>
    <l n="15">qui periculum amat, in illud</l>
    <l n="16">incidat, &amp; qui gladio ferit,</l>
    <l n="17">gladio pereat. Deinde miser</l>
    <l n="18">est, quod ejus vestigia, quem</l>
    <l n="19">odio habet, imitetur, &amp; ad ejus</l>
    <l n="20">exemplum sese obvertat. Et</l>
    <l n="21">quem pessimum judicat, suo</l>
    <l n="22">collaudet facto, ejusque iniqua</l>
    <l n="23">opera approbet. Ex adverso,</l>
    <l n="24">Deum quem optimum novit,</l>
    <l n="25">quem amat, saltem quem a-</l>
    <l n="26">mare sejactitat, deserat, nec ad</l>
  </main_text>
  <notes>The first word "riculo" is a fragment continuing from the previous page and is kept as a fragment. Catchword "ejus" is at the foot right and is not repeated in the text. The word "sejactitat" may be printed with a different first letter; the scan is faint there. Some stains and small marks in the margins are not printed text and are omitted.</notes>
